From: huhucapture maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] screencast: include the declaration of close

The fixed 0.8.1 source calls close() in xdpw_wlr_screencopy_finish()
without including unistd.h. Ubuntu 24.04's host development headers do
not supply that declaration transitively. Include its POSIX header;
retain -Werror and all capture/transport behavior.

Source: emersion/xdg-desktop-portal-wlr
Commit: e1d5d16f0e064a0b788c5d70c11461b15ee7a4af
License: MIT (the original LICENSE remains with the source/build)

diff --git a/src/screencast/wlr_screencast.c b/src/screencast/wlr_screencast.c
--- a/src/screencast/wlr_screencast.c
+++ b/src/screencast/wlr_screencast.c
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
 #include <sys/mman.h>
 #include <sys/param.h>
 #include <sys/stat.h>
+#include <unistd.h>
 #include <assert.h>
 #include <wayland-client-protocol.h>
 #include <xf86drm.h>
